>Some comments:
>3.1 seems to have FAR more gold in it than 3.0 ever did. Have you noticed
>that your pet will now pick up gold too? 

Actually I've found far LESS gold. There is a *LOT* more magic though, esp.
potions of healing, extra healing, and gain level. Also a lot of scrolls
of teleportation and wands of teleportation/digging. In my current game
I have so many wands of t-port I just leave them lying around... monsters
don't USUALLY get to use them anyway. A +5 rustproof Frost Brand usually
only requires 2 hits...

Also I've found its easier to gain levels. I have a 15th level Barbarian
(finished Quest & killed Medusa. Castle is next) and I often finished 3.0
with lower level characters!

One more thing- attributes are *MUCH* harder to gain. I didn't get cold
resistance until I ate my 3rd or 4th Yeti (plus one or two blue jellies) and
I *STILL* haven't gotten fire resistance (eaten a Red Naga and a couple molds).
This is starting to worry me with Hell coming up....

>I REALLY like the new pet behaviour as well. I usually abondoned my pet

I'd like to second this...

>Just how big are the Gnome mines anyway? I've been down about 5 levels worth
>now and still not found the bottom (I have this dying problem you see... ).

My current game they went from dungeon level 3 (main dungeon) down to 10. So
that's 7 levels. The Mine Town was at about level 7 (5th level of Mines).

As for dying- I suggest tackling a few extra "normal" levels before going
into the mines. The mines have too many creatures for low level characters.

